.\" Title: vrc-kill
.\" Author: vrc contributors
.\" Manual section: 1
.\"
.TH VRL\-KILL 1 "2025" "vrc" "User Commands"

.SH NAME
vrc\-kill \- stop (kill) a command inside a running instance

.SH SYNOPSIS
.B vrc
\fBkill\fR \fIPID\fR [\fB\-c\fR \fICOMMAND\fR] [\fB\-\-interactive\fR]

.SH DESCRIPTION
Stop (kill) a specific command inside a running vrc instance. This sends a graceful kill request (SIGINT followed by SIGKILL after the configured \fB\-\-exit\-timeout\fR) to the command, allowing it to clean up resources before termination.

This is the vrc equivalent of vrw's \fBvrw stop\-command\fR. The key difference is that vrc targets a specific instance by PID and command ID, while vrw can search across all instances.

Connects to the target instance's UDS control socket at \fB~/.local/share/vrc/control\-{pid}.sock\fR.

Note: \fBvrc stop\fR stops an entire instance (all commands). \fBvrc kill\fR stops a single command within an instance.

.SH ARGUMENTS

.TP
.B PID
OS process ID of the target vrc instance.

.SH OPTIONS

.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-command " " \fICOMMAND\fR
ID of the target command (omit for the first/only command).

.TP
.BR \-\-interactive
Present a numbered list of all running commands in the instance and allow the user to select one or more by number (space-separated). Overrides \-c.

.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print help information and exit.

.SH EXAMPLES

.PP
Kill the only command in an instance:
.RS
.PP
.nf
\fB$ vrc kill 12345\fR
Command cmd_abc killed
.fi
.RE

.PP
Kill a specific command by ID:
.RS
.PP
.nf
\fB$ vrc kill 12345 \-c cmd_def\fR
.fi
.RE

.PP
Interactively select commands to kill:
.RS
.PP
.nf
\fB$ vrc kill 12345 \-\-interactive\fR
  1) htop (PID 5678)
  2) vim notes.txt (PID 5679)
  3) cargo build (PID 5680)
Select [space-separated numbers]: 1 3
Command cmd_abc killed
Command cmd_ghi killed
.fi
.RE

.SH EXIT STATUS

.TP
.B 0
Command killed successfully.

.TP
.B 1
Error (instance not found, command not found, etc.).

.SH SEE ALSO
.BR vrc (1),
.BR vrc\-stop (1),
.BR vrc\-list (1),
.BR vrc\-freeze (1),
.BR kill (1)
